patrone-settings (0.3.0) resolute; urgency=medium

  * The title bar buttons' style is a setting of its own (title-buttons):
    Wide, Round, Dots, Glossy, or the theme's own. Each style sets every
    part of the buttons in every state, so libadwaita apps, other GTK 4
    apps and GTK 3 apps look the same; before, the buttons looked
    different from one app to the next, and some vanished. Themes keep only
    their title bars (Classic's and Royal's).
  * --set-title-buttons STYLE, and --apply, which an autostart entry runs at
    every sign-in so every account has the styles, and gets new versions
    of them.

 -- William Daugherty <31995458+billsecond@users.noreply.github.com>  Mon, 26 Oct 2026 23:30:00 -0500

patrone-settings (0.2.0) resolute; urgency=medium

  * The Taskbar page also sets the layout (Left, Centered, Split with Start
    on the left and the apps in the middle, or Top) and the Start button's
    icon (eight to pick from). Themes no longer move the taskbar's buttons.
  * Royal: the old Classic, glossy royal blue with a green Start button, no
    longer saying "start". Classic is now plain and square, with solid
    title bars.
  * --set-theme THEME applies a theme without a window, and
    --export-previews DIR saves the choices' pictures; the package installs
    them in /usr/share/patrone/settings/previews. GNOME Settings' Patrone
    page uses both.

 -- William Daugherty <31995458+billsecond@users.noreply.github.com>  Mon, 26 Oct 2026 23:00:00 -0500

patrone-settings (0.1.0) resolute; urgency=medium

  * First package: Patrone Settings, with a Taskbar page (small, medium or
    large), a Title bar buttons page (top right or top left) and a Theme
    page (Patrone, Modern, Classic, Studio), each choice with a picture.
    Themes restyle the taskbar, and title bars and window buttons in GTK 3
    and GTK 4 apps, through the account's gtk.css.

 -- William Daugherty <31995458+billsecond@users.noreply.github.com>  Mon, 26 Oct 2026 17:30:00 -0500
